- Uses the cold bath (8°C) that has shown high pore fractions
- Increases wait time from 200s to 300s (longer evaporation may increase modulus without collapsing pores)
- Reuses the proven mixing_temp=45, pullcast_speed=7, N2=true combination
- Is distinct from existing points (no experiment at bath_temp=8, polymer_wt=14.5)

This is a genuine exploration point targeting a Pareto improvement: potentially higher modulus than the 14p5/10°C runs while maintaining high pore fraction.

