[2026-10-19 19:25:50] LLM suggestion: ## Analysis

### Pareto Front Assessment

Reviewing all experiments for the two objectives (Elastic Modulus, Pore Fraction), the non-dominated candidates are those where no other experiment beats both simultaneously. Key observations:

| Condition | Modulus (bar) | Pore Fraction | Quality |
|---|---|---|---|
| 14-0add-8deg-N2-1250s (run1) | 103.6 | 0.75 | minor creases |
| 14-0add-8deg-N2-1250s (run2) | 189.4 | 0.71 | clean |
| 14-0add-8deg-N2-1250s (run3) | 171.5 | 0.63 | top gap |
| 14-0add-8deg-N2-1250s (run4) | 246.0 | 0.57 | clean |
| 14p8-17deg-N2-1425s (run2) | 217.0 | **0.82** | wrinkles |
| 14p8-17deg-N2-1425s (run3) | 287.9 | 0.63 | wrinkle |
| 14p8-17deg-N2-1425s (run4) | 259.7 | 0.44 | clean |
| 14p5-10deg-N2-1500s (run1) | 222.3 | 0.67 | clean |
| 14p5-10deg-N2-1500s (run2) | 209.1 | 0.69 | clean |
| 14p5-10deg-N2-1500s (run3) | 255.5 | 0.66 | top gap |
| 14p5-8deg-N2-1500s | 189.6 | 0.63 | clean |
| 17-13deg-N2-1800s (run2) | 354.4 | 0.61 | coverage gaps |
| 13-20deg-N2-1550s | 147.8 | 0.65 | top gap |

The **14p5-10deg-N2-1500s** condition (polymer_wt=14.5, bath_temp=10, mixing_temp=45, pullcast_speed=7, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=200, nips_bath_wait_time=1500) has two clean, well-formed runs with modulus ~210–222 bar and pore fraction ~0.67–0.69. This is a strong Pareto-front candidate combining high pore fraction with moderate-to-good modulus. Run 3 showed a top gap, so reproducibility is uncertain.

The **14p8-17deg-N2-1425s run2** showed pore fraction 0.82 (highest observed) with modulus 217 bar — but had wrinkles. Run 3 gave 0.63/288 and run 4 gave 0.44/260. The pore fraction is highly variable (0.44–0.82), suggesting the 0.82 may be an outlier or wrinkle-influenced measurement. This condition needs more data.

### Validation Policy Check

- **14p5-10deg-N2-1500s**: 3 runs exist (runs 1, 2, 3). Runs 1 and 2 are clean with consistent pore fraction (~0.67–0.69) and modulus (~209–222 bar). Run 3 had a top gap and slightly higher modulus (255) but same pore fraction range. Two clean independent runs are consistent — this is approaching confirmed but run 3's gap introduces uncertainty. A 4th clean run would confirm.

- **14p8-17deg-N2-1425s**: 3 runs with highly variable pore fraction (0.44, 0.63, 0.82) and wrinkle issues in runs 2 and 3. Run 4 was clean but gave low pore fraction. This condition is not reproducibly high on pore fraction.

### Decision

The **14p5-10deg-N2-1500s** condition is the strongest current Pareto-front candidate for balanced high modulus + high pore fraction, with two clean runs showing consistent ~0.68 pore fraction and ~215 bar modulus. A 4th independent repeat will confirm synthesis reproducibility before treating it as a confirmed improvement. This is the correct next step per validation policy.

